WEBVTT

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:39.473
The Isle of Sky Sky is an island off the north-west coast of Scotland.

00:00:39.532 --> 00:00:48.776
It is the largest and most well-known of the inner hebrides, and many people think it looks like a big butterfly.

00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:59.981
It is 25 miles wide and 50 miles long, and it is often called by its poetic name Eilanejo.

00:01:00.041 --> 00:01:05.724
Sky is famous for its natural beauty, history and wildlife.

00:01:05.783 --> 00:01:14.268
Climbers and walkers love going into the coolen hills and on-sky you are never far from the sea.

00:01:14.328 --> 00:01:25.584
The wildlife ranges from magnificent golden eagle to red deer and if you're lucky you can see otters playing on the shores.

00:01:25.644 --> 00:01:33.410
As you travel around the island it is possible to hear Scottish Gaelic which is the local language.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:37.744
and you can find Gaelic culture everywhere.

00:01:37.804 --> 00:01:40.996
Sky is very beautiful.

00:01:41.056 --> 00:01:52.222
There are hillsides, locks, lakes, whitewashed cottages, lots of sheep, but almost no people.

00:01:52.282 --> 00:02:01.136
Many years ago, the inhabitants were highland chieftains, lords or lairs who lived in castles.

00:02:01.196 --> 00:02:06.968
but now they are farmers or crafters and fishermen on the coasts.

00:02:07.028 --> 00:02:18.010
There are shopkeepers and teachers who live and work in the main towns of Broadford and Potry, but most people on Sky live simply.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:26.447
They are families who love the land of their fathers.

00:02:26.507 --> 00:02:35.395
I pulled the curtains open and looked down at the street.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:42.477
It was hot, too hot for London in the middle of July and I was angry.

00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:47.258
I closed the curtains and returned to my mother's room.

00:02:47.318 --> 00:02:51.760
She lay in bed and I could hear her breathing.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:57.607
She looked so thin and I sat next to her and held her hand.

00:02:57.667 --> 00:03:00.604
I'm not going," I said.

00:03:00.664 --> 00:03:02.525
You can't send me away.

00:03:02.545 --> 00:03:09.878
I looked at my mother and her face was white like the sheets and pillowcases.

00:03:09.938 --> 00:03:15.352
It's only for a month until I feel a little better, my darling.

00:03:15.412 --> 00:03:19.254
She said, then you can come home.

00:03:19.314 --> 00:03:23.366
Dr. Barnes stood on the other side of the bed.

00:03:23.426 --> 00:03:26.382
Has Meghan got any friends?

00:03:26.442 --> 00:03:30.359
He asked Mrs. Brown our home help.

00:03:30.418 --> 00:03:33.100
Mrs. Brown shook her head.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.181
Meghan doesn't have any friends.

00:03:36.241 --> 00:03:38.152
I heard her whisper.

00:03:38.212 --> 00:03:40.752
She's a strange child.

00:03:40.812 --> 00:03:42.233
Friends?

00:03:42.293 --> 00:03:45.275
Of course I didn't have any friends.

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:52.471
We moved to this part of London six months ago and my new school was horrible.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.045
Mother didn't know.

00:03:54.065 --> 00:04:00.210
I didn't tell her about the bullies and the nasty text messages.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:03.474
Dr. Barnes put his glasses on.

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:07.146
I could see that he didn't know what to do.

00:04:07.206 --> 00:04:10.179
We needed a miracle.

00:04:10.239 --> 00:04:13.522
Your mother is very unwell, Meghan.

00:04:13.582 --> 00:04:14.904
He said.

00:04:14.964 --> 00:04:19.752
She needs to rest, and you can't stay here for the summer holidays.

00:04:19.812 --> 00:04:22.588
I don't want to leave you mum.

00:04:22.648 --> 00:04:27.952
You want to send me to the Highlands of Scotland to stay with Uncle Fraser.

00:04:28.012 --> 00:04:30.984
But I hate the countryside.

00:04:31.044 --> 00:04:34.246
I stood up and looked at the doctor.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:38.479
I'm not going and you can't make me go.

00:04:38.539 --> 00:04:41.871
But Dr Barnes could make me go.

00:04:41.931 --> 00:04:46.536
And he did.

00:04:46.595 --> 00:04:55.602
I watched the countryside change through the window of the train as we travelled into Scotland.

00:04:55.662 --> 00:05:01.506
I could see fields, dry stone walls and lots of sheep.

00:05:01.566 --> 00:05:04.918
But where were the people?

00:05:04.977 --> 00:05:10.480
Mrs Wallace, a friend of Dr Barnes was with me.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.665
She wanted to chat, but I didn't.

00:05:14.724 --> 00:05:18.038
The Isle of Skye is beautiful.

00:05:18.098 --> 00:05:21.800
The air is so fresh," she said.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.030
I hate fresh air.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.382
I like the air in London.

00:05:26.441 --> 00:05:28.083
I said.

00:05:28.142 --> 00:05:32.264
Mrs. Wallace sighed and opened her book.

00:05:32.324 --> 00:05:37.386
We changed trains, and the next one was very old.

00:05:37.446 --> 00:05:41.258
A man sat singing quietly in the corner.

00:05:41.318 --> 00:05:44.224
He had a long white beard.

00:05:44.284 --> 00:05:49.530
In another corner, there was a woman with a basket of chickens.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:52.442
I looked at these people.

00:05:52.502 --> 00:05:55.564
I came from a different world.

00:05:55.624 --> 00:06:01.208
In my world, there were shops, people, and traffic.

00:06:01.268 --> 00:06:04.209
We caught the ferry at Malik.

00:06:04.269 --> 00:06:11.354
The wind blew my long dark hair, and my pale blue eyes searched the island for people.

00:06:11.414 --> 00:06:14.008
But it looked so quiet.

00:06:14.068 --> 00:06:19.732
Cloud Island said Mrs. Wallace, giving me a sweet.

00:06:19.792 --> 00:06:24.583
In the Old North language, ski means cloud.

00:06:24.643 --> 00:06:27.183
And I means island.

00:06:27.243 --> 00:06:29.814
It's often misty here.

00:06:29.874 --> 00:06:32.074
I didn't answer.

00:06:32.134 --> 00:06:35.855
I could only think that I wanted to go home.

00:06:35.915 --> 00:06:43.278
We got off the ferried Armadale, and I stood by the sea and waited for my uncle.

00:06:43.338 --> 00:06:46.681
I felt wrong in my London clothes.

00:06:46.741 --> 00:06:51.842
I took my mobile phone out of my pocket and called home.

00:06:51.902 --> 00:06:56.193
Mrs. Brown answered, but mum was asleep.

00:06:56.253 --> 00:06:58.354
Your uncle's here?

00:06:58.414 --> 00:07:00.384
Said Mrs. Wallace.

00:07:00.444 --> 00:07:02.454
I said goodbye.

00:07:02.514 --> 00:07:03.975
Meghan.

00:07:04.035 --> 00:07:06.365
A strong voice called.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:11.726
He was a tall man with wavy hair and a big smile.

00:07:11.786 --> 00:07:13.742
I'm over here.

00:07:13.802 --> 00:07:16.899
He disappeared behind some trees.

00:07:16.959 --> 00:07:20.130
Pulling my suitcase I followed.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:23.071
But my uncle didn't have a car.

00:07:23.131 --> 00:07:33.355
He was standing next to a beige colored pony and he put my suitcase into a little red trap.

00:07:33.415 --> 00:07:38.296
Listening activity.

00:07:38.356 --> 00:07:40.488
One.

00:07:40.547 --> 00:07:42.900
