00:08:20.201 --> 00:08:24.035
Chapter Two.

00:08:24.094 --> 00:08:26.746
The Croft.

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:35.872
The journey was uncomfortable in the Ponian Trap as we trotted along the narrow roads, but it was fun too.

00:08:35.932 --> 00:08:42.510
I could see the bay, the seaweed and the rocks, and smell the salty sea.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:45.315
Seagulls flew overhead.

00:08:45.374 --> 00:08:47.506
I looked at my uncle.

00:08:47.566 --> 00:08:51.718
He had my mother's smile, but they were very different.

00:08:51.778 --> 00:08:54.430
He saw me looking at him.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:58.992
So, this is your first visit to Skye Meghan.

00:08:59.052 --> 00:09:01.323
I'm so pleased you're here.

00:09:01.383 --> 00:09:07.366
He said, I want to bring Mum next time when she's better, I said.

00:09:07.426 --> 00:09:09.898
His eyes look sad.

00:09:09.958 --> 00:09:13.338
I want her to come here too.

00:09:13.398 --> 00:09:18.108
And then he took a deep breath, and there was silence.

00:09:18.168 --> 00:09:25.554
We trotted on through a forest, and then we stopped at a place where the view of the mountains was spectacular.

00:09:25.614 --> 00:09:27.394
The Kulin Range?

00:09:27.454 --> 00:09:29.286
Said Uncle Fraser.

00:09:29.346 --> 00:09:33.108
This is the best place to see the mountains.

00:09:33.168 --> 00:09:36.540
I got out of the trap and looked around.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.774
It was a magical place.

00:09:38.834 --> 00:09:43.288
There was a ruined castle, and below a sandy beach.

00:09:43.348 --> 00:09:50.012
The waves crashed, and I thought I saw a silvery white horse playing in the water.

00:09:50.072 --> 00:09:55.276
It ran and jumped, and I am sure that I heard it call me.

00:09:55.336 --> 00:09:57.368
Uncle Fraser!

00:09:57.428 --> 00:10:01.472
I shouted, there's a white horse!

00:10:01.531 --> 00:10:07.770
He didn't hear me, and when I turned, the silvery white horse was not there.

00:10:07.829 --> 00:10:10.195
We got into the trap.

00:10:10.254 --> 00:10:13.826
I saw a silvery white horse down by the sea.

00:10:13.886 --> 00:10:19.580
I said Uncle Fraser stopped and looked at me with surprise.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.140
Did you?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:24.973
But then he said no more.

00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:28.666
My mobile phone beeped.

00:10:28.726 --> 00:10:31.668
You have one new message it said.

00:10:31.728 --> 00:10:34.268
I pressed read.

00:10:34.328 --> 00:10:36.866
Have a sad holiday.

00:10:36.926 --> 00:10:39.452
I pressed eliminate.

00:10:39.512 --> 00:10:42.974
It was from one of the horrible girls at school.

00:10:43.034 --> 00:10:45.054
I switched my phone off.

00:10:45.114 --> 00:10:47.616
I needed to forget about them.

00:10:47.676 --> 00:10:50.757
The roads were very narrow now.

00:10:50.818 --> 00:10:52.998
We are nearly home.

00:10:53.058 --> 00:10:54.789
Said my uncle.

00:10:54.849 --> 00:10:56.810
I stared at him.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:59.131
We couldn't be nearly home.

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:01.488
We were in the countryside.

00:11:01.548 --> 00:11:08.910
I could see some small houses, lots of animals and grass, but there was no town.

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:13.052
Uncle Fraser turned right into a small track.

00:11:13.113 --> 00:11:14.964
Home, Darwin.

00:11:15.024 --> 00:11:17.796
Uncle Fraser said to the pony.

00:11:17.856 --> 00:11:23.068
Darwin walked slowly because there were chickens running in front of him.

00:11:23.128 --> 00:11:29.530
At the end of the track, there was a little white house with a front garden full of flowers.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:35.530
In one field, I could see four cows waiting patiently by the gate.

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:39.362
And in another, there were some goats and a donkey.

00:11:39.422 --> 00:11:40.733
We're home.

00:11:40.793 --> 00:11:42.554
Said Uncle Fraser.

00:11:42.614 --> 00:11:47.757
Welcome to White Heather Cottage.

00:11:47.818 --> 00:11:51.390
